  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Since the networked IK update, changes to object sync's networking behaviour have caused objects teleported with the TeleportTo RPC to interpolate their position for non-owners of objects.\nA similar effect can be seen on players, but the effect on object synced objects can create two major problems:\n\n- Teleported objects cam enter a resting state prematurely for non-owners after the owner sees it go into a sleeping state.  Remote players who have yet to fully interpolate the object to its new position cam evem see an object stop mid-air if the network conditions are right.\n- Teleported objects can accidentally interact with world objects/triggers in between their original position and their teleport target position for non-owners.  This can cause evem further problems with triggers in complex worlds.\n\nwrld_ba469322-1303-4bb6-af71-b750aaef7c75 is a test world that demonstrates both of these problems.  The two white buttons teleport the pickup to two different locations, and the blue trigger volume plays an audio source for everyone and teleports the pickup to a third position if it enters the volume.\n\nOne change to the networking behaviour that could solve both of these problems is a specific flag within the networking protocol that signifies a teleport RPC, and doesn't interpolate an object's change in position once received.",
